{
  "$comment": "The leagues' boosted drops (Wiki: Trailblazer_Reloaded_League/Boosted_drops and Raging_Echoes_League/Boosted_drops, read 2026-10-26; Demonic_Pacts_League/Boosted_drops and the Demonic_Pacts_League/Areas/<area>/Notable_drops subpages it transcludes, read 2026-11-01), applied by plugins/modes/league/BoostedDrops.LeagueMode.js with the rate in leagues.json `passives.dropRate`. Each source is a Wiki row group: `npcs` are the NPC names whose kills it covers (an NpcDrops kill asks `npc-drops:chance` with the NPC's name), `items` the drops it boosts (names as the drop tables carry them; the Wiki's group rows - 'Armadyl armour', 'Any Godsword shard', 'Barrows armour pieces' - are expanded by hand), `leagues` restricts a row to the leagues (4 Trailblazer Reloaded, 5 Raging Echoes, 6 Demonic Pacts) whose page lists it (all when absent). A source without `npcs` is rolled by its own plugin (a chest, a raid, a minigame, pickpocketing), which can ask `drops:chance` with the source's `name` (or pass it as `source` on `npc-drops:roll-table`); until it does the row is inert. `rollers` are the pages' Global entries: every unique of that roller. Rows the pages mark N/A (the echo bosses' uniques, Skotizo's uncut onyx, mogre flippers) are left out. Where a page says an item drops completed (Demonic Pacts' DT2 rings, Eternal boots, Ancient sceptre, Confliction gauntlets), the row also names the parts this server's tables drop. A name is matched whole without case; `/.../` is a regular expression (without case); `*` matches everything.",
